# -------------------------------------------------------------------- ways ---
# How you get from deck to deck, as built and as the war left it.
#
# As built: the ladder. It stands against the north wall of the shaft, the
# whole way up, with a landing at every deck door. The piece is one voxel tall
# and stacks, so a run is one line: where it starts, and how many voxels of it.
#
# `at` names the tile it stands in, not the wall it stands against -
# genladder's own wallZ pushes the model to the local +Z edge of that tile, so
# the position is the tile's centre (a half, like every other entity's is) and
# `facing=0,1` turns the model's own +Z to face world -Z, which is the only
# way the push lands the rails against a wall on the tile's north side instead
# of stranding them in mid-air on its south one.
#
# The six pressurised decks, D1's floor to D6's ceiling.
entity Ladder mesh=ladder at=80.5,116,79.5 facing=0,1 step=0,1,0 times=14
# The vacuum decks above the upper hatch, as far as the run survived: D7 and
# D8, and then nothing, because the rest of it went with the residences.
entity Ladder mesh=ladder at=80.5,131,79.5 facing=0,1 step=0,1,0 times=5
# The engineering decks, the reactor gallery to the hatch under D1, less the
# stretch the mass tanks took with them when they tore loose.
entity Ladder mesh=ladder at=80.5,35,79.5 facing=0,1 step=0,1,0 times=28
entity Ladder mesh=ladder at=80.5,79,79.5 facing=0,1 step=0,1,0 times=36

# What the war did to it. Two plugs of wreckage in the shaft, which is what
# "partially obstructed" means here: the ladder is still there behind them and
# it no longer gets you through.
#
# Between D3 and D4, where the mess deck came down into the shaft.
fill scorch 79 122 79 81 122 81
# Between D8 and D9, under the hole the hydroponics blast tore upwards.
fill scorch 79 136 79 81 137 81
# And the run above D9 is simply gone, which is why there are no rungs past
# y=139: out there the suit is the way up.

# What it opened instead.
#
# The mess floor fell into the service cabins below it, and somebody rigged a
# ladder up through the hole. It is the only way between D3 and D4 now.
clear 84 122 68 86 122 70
entity Ladder mesh=ladder at=85.5,121,68.5 facing=0,1 step=0,1,0 times=2
# Above the plug at D8, the hydroponics hole is the way: it goes from the farm
# deck up through the staff flats into the residences, and it was already
# there - see the damage section. From D9 up, the promenade's blown-out glass
# and the bridge's vents are open to space, so the suit goes round the outside.

