# ------------------------------------------------------------------ plate ---
# The ship's own wayfinding plate, on the lab wall the player wakes up facing,
# beside the door out: the whole ark in section, every deck named, and a mark
# on deck six saying where the reader is standing. It is the one thing in the
# level that shows how the eleven decks, the drum and the drive fit together -
# the signs by the ladder only ever name the deck they are on.
#
# The drawing is baked into the model (tools/genpanels, ark_chart.go), so it is
# a piece of scenery like a table and knows nothing about the game. It also
# knows nothing about the war: it was screwed to this wall when the ship was
# new, and says the shaft runs bridge to reactor gallery because it did. The
# red signs and Reyes are what tell you otherwise.
entity ArkChart mesh=ark_chart at=83.03,128,72.5 facing=1,0
# A lamp over it, because signage on a ship is lit and a plate this size in
# the dark is a grey rectangle.
light 85.5 129.6 72.5 color=0.85,0.95,1 power=4 baked
sign 58.03 116 78.5 1,0 !AIRLOCK|VACUUM BEYOND
sign 78.5 125 103.97 0,-1 !AIRLOCK|VACUUM BEYOND

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- guides ---
# Two orientation holograms, standing either side of where the player wakes
# in the lab. Both offer a tour; agree, and the one you asked leads off along
# its own route, waiting at each leg for the player to catch up rather than
# talking to an empty corridor - see Actor.startTour. Purser was recorded
# before the war and does not know it happened; Reyes was recorded after, and
# is not telling.
#
# A guide walks a straight line leg by leg rather than through the ordinary
# A* pathfinder (see updateTour's own comment for why that system cannot find
# a floor anywhere on this deck at all), so each leg has to be a clear,
# axis-aligned corridor rather than anywhere the map is walkable - every one
# below was checked against the compiled map.bin before being written here.
#
# And every waypoint is a tile *centre*, the half like every other entity's
# position: a whole number is the seam between two tiles, and a guide walking
# a seam is a guide with half its body in whatever the neighbouring tile holds.
# That is what walked them through the spine's wall on the way in - the deck
# door is one tile wide and the leg ran down its edge.
#
# Purser crosses the lab into the spine shaft and stands where the ladder up
# is - as far as he is concerned, the way to the bridge. Reyes crosses into
# the gene vault corridor and comes back east along it to stand under the
# "DECK 7 SEALED" sign, the current route's own dead end.
entity Purser at=85.0,128,70.5 facing=1,0  sprite=actors/humans/scientist_hologram patrol=84.5,128,70.5;84.5,128,80.5;80.5,128,80.5
entity Reyes  at=92.0,128,70.5 facing=-1,0 sprite=actors/humans/scientist_hologram patrol=76.5,128,70.5;76.5,128,83.5;80.5,128,83.5

